    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>“Fire insurance adjuster” can mean three different people: a staff adjuster or independent adjuster (both working for the insurer), or a public adjuster (working for you).</li>
<li>Fire claims usually include more than burned materials. Smoke, soot, firefighting water, contents, and living expenses all need separate documentation.</li>
<li>Do not discard damaged items or begin major demolition until the damage is documented.</li>
<li>Texas regulates public adjusters under Insurance Code Chapter 4102. Fees are capped at 10% of the settlement, and you have 72 hours to rescind a contract.</li>
